<ul>
  <li><strong>Owner</strong>: everything, including billing, exporting data and closing the account.</li>
  <li><strong>Manager</strong>: runs the shop: products and prices, stock, purchasing, customers, reports, and approving discounts and voids.</li>
  <li><strong>Cashier</strong>: sells, takes payments and does returns at the till.</li>
  <li><strong>Stock clerk</strong>: receives deliveries, moves stock between branches and counts it.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Quick switching with a PIN</h2>
<p>On a shared till, staff don't need to sign out. Each person sets a 4 to 6 digit PIN under <strong>My profile</strong>, then <strong>Switch user</strong> changes who's selling in a couple of taps.</p>

<h2>Discounts that need approval</h2>
<p>Cashiers can give discounts up to the limit set in <strong>Settings → Shop</strong>. Anything bigger asks for a manager's approval PIN at the till.</p>

<h2>Two-factor sign-in</h2>
<p>Owners and managers should turn on two-factor sign-in under <strong>My profile</strong>, using an authenticator app. The owner can require it for all managers.</p>
